WEBVTT

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.790
Let's go!

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.790
Fight, yeah! Fight, yeah! Fight, yeah!

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:22.450
"Ionodai at Nagano Prefecture
training camp..."

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.870
There he goes again...

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.660
No improvement.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.120
Remember to pace yourself.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.410
Hey, outta gas already?

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.830
Not yet!

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.830
Ken, don't overdo it.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.790
Is this déjà vu?

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.790
As ever, you need to work on
your basic physical fitness.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.870
You're a lap behind.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.370
Shut it! I can do... the run...

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.290
Quality over quantity, remember?

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.540
There's a difference
when you don't have a trainer.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.910
Come on, now. How long will you rest for?

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.500
You'll never finish like that.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.620
Dammit! I'll show you!

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.950
The Grand Prix Series for High School
Skate-Leading is just around the corner.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.410
This training camp is the key
to making it to the finals.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:13.830
What?

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.160
You're so handsome when
you're thinking serious thoughts.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.160
Stop it.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.500
"Episode 5
Bonds"

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.250
This year's Grand Prix Series opens soon.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:03.620
Needless to say, we're aiming to win nationals.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.200
To achieve that, we need
to first make it to the finals.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.830
None of you want to shed tears because
we missed qualifying by 0.01 points, right?

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.290
We <i>will</i> qualify for the finals.
We'll earn every point we can get.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.910
Have that in mind as you
undertake this training camp!

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:17.950
--Yes, sir!
--Yessir!

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.160
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.080
Maeshima, don't tell me you don't
know the rules for the series.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.910
Uh, we just have to win, right...?

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:25.830
Wh--?!

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.790
No? But we've got to win--

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.160
Right, listen up.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.830
The Grand Prix Series for High School
Skate-Leading has a total of eight matches.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:33.080
"6 Seeded Teams"

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:33.080
The Grand Prix Series for High School
Skate-Leading has a total of eight matches.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.500
"6 Seeded Teams"

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.500
The six schools from the
finals last year are seeded.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.000
"6 Seeded Teams           "10 Teams From Preliminaries"

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.000
Add the ten schools who make it through
preliminaries for a total of 16 schools,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.080
"6 Seeded Teams           "10 Teams From Preliminaries"

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.080
who each compete in three of the eight matches.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.870
"6 Seeded Teams           "10 Teams From Preliminaries"

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.870
The six schools with the highest
scores qualify for the finals.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.790
"6 Seeded Teams           "10 Teams From Preliminaries"

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.790
This also ensures they're seeded
in next year's competition.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:55.040
Then the top-scoring school at the finals
becomes that year's champion.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.120
Got it?

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.830
You could've saved your breath.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:03.160
We've been assigned to compete
in the first match in Shizuoka next month.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.290
And Shinozaki?

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.540
St. Clavis starts in the third match.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.160
Lucky us. We don't have to compete
against the favorite right off the bat.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.620
That's no fun.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.160
Don't let your guard down. In the first match,

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.580
we'll be up against Chutei University
Kamimaezu High, who came sixth last year.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:23.910
Perfect unison. A team known for their
precision and perfect synchronization.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:28.120
The Ishikawa brothers, their twin aces,
further boost their prowess.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:32.160
They achieve pretty high scores for style,
and of course, their technical is perfect.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.290
They're an infallible powerhouse.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.160
But we don't plan on losing to any team.

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.830
Let's win this first match!

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:40.910
--Yes!
--Yeah!

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.790
The coach has assigned our music and formation.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:49.000
You'll learn the choreography for
each position during this training camp.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.660
I'll now announce the starting team.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.000
First, the guards... will be Jonouchi and me.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.120
Huh? Got it!

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:56.950
What's the matter?

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:57.870
Nothing.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.700
I bet he was hoping for lead.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.950
Wing, Akimitsu Mochizuki.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.080
Okay.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.160
Lead, Kiriyama.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.330
Okay.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:10.620
And the other lead... Maeshima.
Tomo will be on reserve.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.790
All right! It was obvious, though!

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.080
You seem ecstatic, considering.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.750
Weren't you actually a little nervous?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.370
I was not!

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.160
Your individual technique is important,

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.910
but since this is team figure skating,
teamwork is vital.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.580
Don't forget that.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.540
Okay!

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.830
What a surprise.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.660
Weren't those Ionodai students?

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.410
Why are they here?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.620
They're a public school, you know?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.500
I can finally train on the rink!

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.250
Don't go too crazy.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.040
You should be pretty fatigued
from running those mountain trails.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.660
Just get the feeling back today.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.870
Sure thing.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.580
Hm? What are you doing, Kubota?

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.750
U-Um, I thought I could act
as support for Akimitsu...

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:56.330
Though you're on reserve,
you're still on the team.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.370
Don't do support work, go practice.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.040
I've got this part covered.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.790
You're a lead. Got that?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.830
Yes, sir!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:10.620
Come on, you're going too wide!
Keep it tighter and get the timing right!

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.160
But it's cooler my way.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.620
It's not about being cool!
You need to focus on position and timing!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.500
Whether it's cool or not
is the most important, Itsuki!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.450
That's "Kiriyama, sir" to you!

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.040
Enough. Tomo, take his place.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.080
I want to do a full run-through
to review the performance.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.580
Y-Yes, sir.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:31.410
You can practice with me instead!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.830
Tomo, don't go along with Master Four-Eyes.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.120
Practice with me.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.120
Cut it out!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.950
What's your problem?

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.040
Tomo, what are you laughing at?

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.540
What do you have up your sleeve?

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:47.160
For you to assign our music and routine...

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.950
Has your sense of duty awakened?

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:54.700
Just self-preservation. I've got to show
that I'm doing the bare minimum.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.750
Oh?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:02.160
I'd like to change the routine slightly.
Will you suggest it to the team for me?

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.000
Why don't you propose it yourself?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:09.910
They don't fully trust me yet.
Let me aid you in your self-preservation.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:30.410
"Facility's beloved dog. First to arrive
gets to do morning/evening walks!!"

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.870
"On Morning/Evening Walk"

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.200
"Skate Sharpening"

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.200
"Blade Mounting and Positioning"

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.580
He really is good. The breadth of
his interpretation and performance...

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.410
I can only skate as I'm told...

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.910
No! This isn't the time to get depressed.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:21.790
I need to steal as many techniques as I can.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.250
All right, we'll run through
the short program together today.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.700
Starting team, get in the rink.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.950
Okay!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.620
Is this the place?

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.700
How many times do I need to remind you?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.290
Pay attention to your position and timing!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.450
Speak up if you have something to say.
We can't read your mind.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:52.040
I never liked the short program.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.370
Most of the performance is set,
and that makes me restless!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:57.250
Who cares if you like it or not! You--

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.330
Kiriyama.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:03.660
But didn't you used to skate in singles?
Didn't you do a short program then?

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.330
What did you do?

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.660
...ied it.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.250
What was that?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.830
I watched my coach skate and copied it.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.080
What?!

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:17.950
Thinking back, your short program scores
weren't very high in elementary school.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.370
I got top scores when I was really into it!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.120
When you were into it?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:22.910
Are you...

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:23.830
Could it be?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.870
You're no good at the short program?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:27.750
Seriously?

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.080
We discovered an unexpected weakness!

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.910
I-I just don't like all the fine details!

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.790
Everybody has a weakness, right? Say something!

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:38.290
Anyway, let's run through it again.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.700
Maeshima, focus on getting
the choreography down.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.120
Okay...

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.250
You didn't realize, Sasu?

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:53.700
No, I mean, he copies others and... ah!
Then he modifies it as he pleases!

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.870
Hey.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.200
Mr. Miura. What are you doing here?

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.120
I'm here to cover stories
at this training camp site.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.450
On naginata and tennis and such.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.370
We're a poor company.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:16.160
Naturally, I'm in charge of
high school skate-leading, as well.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.580
You think I could come for an interview
sometime tomorrow? For the special issue.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.120
As long as you have the school's consent.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.500
Well? How are they coming along?

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.580
Don't know.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.950
What do you mean you don't know?

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.000
I haven't taught them anything.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.000
Nothing at all?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:36.000
Right there! You weren't together. Again.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.950
Don't waste time, Adachi.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.410
Not yours or that of those kids.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.540
I'm a fan of the figure skater
Takumi Adachi, regardless.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:53.000
Whether you're on the ice or teaching,
I hope to see your personality somewhere.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.330
I'm off. See you at the interview.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:59.410
Okay, now. Stop right there.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:02.410
What's wrong? You don't
seem like yourself, Jonouchi.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.910
He's bummed he wasn't made a lead. Right?

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.250
N-No!

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:10.330
We tend to rely on Terauchi to be a guard.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:14.250
Your physical ability and balance
are valuable and hard to come by.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.660
Well... thanks for that.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:21.120
He was hoping for a lead position
like during the inter-team match.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:28.250
It's hard to alter the formation now,
but the starting team isn't set in stone yet.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:33.080
Got it! In that case, I'll snatch
the position with pure skill.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:36.830
Don't get ahead of yourself and slack
on guard practice because of that.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.200
I'll be fine!

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.290
Jonouchi, I can count on you?

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.040
You bet!

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.080
You should steal Itsuki's starting spot.
Then you can skate with me.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.450
Wh-What?!

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:52.000
You can do it. Wanna compete
in the Grand Prix Series together?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.290
--Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:00.870
--Not happening.
--Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:04.120
My method allows the team
to earn maximum points.

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:07.410
Everything will fall apart
if you go with his method.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.330
I'm not saying you have
to be Maeshima's best friend.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:14.200
Just attempt to find a middle ground
that you can both agree on.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.200
There needs to be some
pressure even within a team.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:23.040
He's a first year,
and we're seniors here, right?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.330
It's for the team. Please.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.290
"Chocolate"

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.290
It's for the team. Please.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:34.700
One, two, three, four.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.500
Maeshima...

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:39.620
One, two, three--

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.790
U-Uh, need something?

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:47.660
Well, Terauchi said... I didn't want to...
but Terauchi wanted me to...

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.080
Maeshima, it's your favorite... Why me?!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.200
What do you want?

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:57.580
Well, uh... Terauchi gave me chocolate
out back... said to talk to you...

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.790
I thought it'd backfire...
if you didn't like it--

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:04.000
Don't come here just to say that.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:08.040
Sorry. Whenever I see his face, I just...

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.750
Well, you can take these things slow.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:12.830
Humiliating...

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.910
I'm really sorry about this.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.910
Oh? Weren't you with the captain?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:24.910
Terauchi and the coach are doing
an interview for the special issue.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.870
It finally feels like the real thing.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.790
Thanks for taking the time out today.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:31.870
Not at all.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:35.540
First, tell me your goal for
this year's Grand Prix Series.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.830
It's the same every year.
We're aiming to be the national champions.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:43.290
It seems Shinozaki has switched to
skate-leading this year. Your thoughts?

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.160
Naturally, we're keeping that in mind.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:51.000
He's joined the St. Clavis team, captained
by Himuro, one of your former teammates?

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.950
Yes. But that doesn't change anything.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.410
In other words?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:59.040
No matter the team,
we consider them rivals to defeat.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.080
I see. How is the team coming together?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.660
The majority of us have skated
together since we were novices,

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.250
so we know each other well.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:09.790
If I recall, all of you but Jonouchi,
who's from Tochigi, were together.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:10.290
Yes. But this is Jonouchi's
second year on the team.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.370
"Sota Jonouchi"    "Tochigi"
"Guard/Wing"

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.370
Yes. But this is Jonouchi's
second year on the team.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:16.830
"Sota Jonouchi"    "Tochigi"
"Guard/Wing"

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:16.830
He's gained a tremendous amount
of strength along with Akimitsu Mochizuki,

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.370
"Sota Jonouchi"    "Tochigi"
"Guard/Wing"

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.370
so there's no issue there.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:22.540
We also have two first years, Kubota and
Maeshima, who have a lot of potential.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.500
They're great additions.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.290
Hear that, Kubota? What do you think?

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:28.750
Huh? Um...

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:31.370
I've known of you since your novice days.

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:34.290
You have a solid grasp of the basics
and perform meticulously.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.290
Your teammates completely
trust in you, too, right?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:37.700
No, I couldn't say that--

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:42.950
It's true. Kubota excels at matching
others and is a reliable skater.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:47.540
His skating style of consistently earning
points is a terrific asset to our team.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.830
Um... that's--

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.330
You heard him, Kubota. You can go.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.200
Oh... yes, sir!

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.450
Let's move on to the next question.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:56.450
Okay.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:15.330
One, two, three, four.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:16.450
--One, two, three, four.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:22.580
--Adachi. You might actually
be pretty good at coaching.
--One, two, three, four.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.040
Maeshima, enough already!

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:27.000
What now?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.330
Oh, no...

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.200
Again. How many times is that today?

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:36.620
We went wider like you wanted.
Why did you still change the timing?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.370
Why did you suddenly go inwards?!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.410
You haven't done it right
once in a run-through yet!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.200
Because I thought it was cooler that way.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.330
That again?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.500
How am I supposed to know if I don't try it?

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.580
How dare you talk like that to an upperclassman?

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:53.500
Don't change the subject!
I want to beat Shinozaki.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.250
Hate me all you want! Just don't drag me down!

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.790
--Wh--!
--Got a problem?!

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.410
Ken.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:00.830
Tomo, you tell him--

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:05.330
That's too much. You know how focused
Kiriyama is on winning, don't you?

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:06.500
Well, but...

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.910
Let's have a match.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.160
What?

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:14.160
Have a match with me, Ken.
We'll do the short program.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.790
Tomo? You...

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:19.580
Kiriyama, sir. If I win,
put me on the starting team.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.700
You serious about this?

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.250
What's going on?

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.910
Shima and Tomo are having a match
for a spot on the starting team.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:37.700
They're skating the short program.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.040
Sasugai...

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.620
Hey, it wasn't me. Kubota's the one
who made the challenge.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:46.410
But you don't seem against it. You think
he'll get an easy win against Tomo?

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:49.410
No way. It might actually be pretty tough.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:55.290
He needs to stop complaining
that it's his weakness.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:17:01.290
We'll skate simultaneously. Whoever ends up
with more points wins. Sound good?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.950
Tomo, if you're mad--

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:04.160
I'm not.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.290
If it's a straight match,
I won't go easy on you.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.500
I know. Give it all you've got.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.950
Yeah, they're both off to a great start.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:24.370
Maeshima's actually following the choreography.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:29.080
And Tomo has strong fundamental skills
since he applies himself during training.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.450
"Tomoyuki Kubota"        "Kensei Maeshima"

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:37.790
It's almost the element that
we argued over being too wide.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.450
What will you do, Maeshima?

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.540
Crap. At this rate, I'll be late
to the next intersection.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.500
See? Skate-leading is a team sport.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.870
"Tomoyuki Kubota"             "Kensei Maeshima"

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.870
See? Skate-leading is a team sport.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.500
"Tomoyuki Kubota"             "Kensei Maeshima"

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.500
As long as you fail to understand that
it's different from singles, Maeshima...

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:56.370
...you'll never beat the well-rounded Tomo!

00:17:56.370 --> 00:18:00.950
Wait, where's the wing supposed
to be right now? And the guard?

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.580
Man, I'm in trouble. Am I going to...

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.790
"Tomoyuki Kubota"                "Kensei Maeshima"

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.500
Kubota's winning.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.080
The gap will just widen if this keeps up.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:14.580
I see. We could remove Maeshima from
the short program and use Tomo instead...

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.200
Yes! I can do this!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.080
You have a solid grasp of the basics
and perform meticulously.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:29.160
...a terrific asset to our team.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:36.000
Meticulously and precisely.
Yes! Like fitting pieces into a puzzle.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.160
The short program suits my skating style!

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:43.500
I'll win if you don't stick to the program, Ken!

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:47.200
Are you kidding? Why can't I catch up to him?

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.450
At this rate...

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.500
"Learn it"

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.830
"Learn it"

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.830
If you learn it, you can replicate it.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:58.080
You can do it, can't you? Learn it, Maeshima.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:01.450
You've got the best example
right in front of you.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:06.790
Tomo, sorry. I'll let you win any other match.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.160
But not this one!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.330
"Tomoyuki Kubota"               "Kensei Maeshima"

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:14.580
Hey, is the difference shrinking?

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.870
Maeshima's catching up.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:19.830
Why? How come?!

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:25.250
I see. By copying Kubota's moves,
he's avoided getting more points deducted.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:28.790
Which means, it comes down
to who has better presentation.

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.540
"Tomoyuki Kubota"               "Kensei Maeshima"

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.450
"Tomoyuki Kubota"               "Kensei Maeshima"

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.450
Shima won, huh?

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:44.450
The captain and the others started
this team when they were first years.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.750
They recruited students with experience.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:51.200
Their first year, people thought
of them as an unofficial club,

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:54.540
but they were narrowly seeded
for the Grand Prix Series

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:59.080
and were finally accepted as an official club.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:03.660
Akimitsu and Jonouchi joined the second year,
and they placed fourth at nationals.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.700
Do you realize how amazing that is?

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:09.120
Yeah, kind of.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.830
I went to watch last year's finals.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.790
"Saitama Prefectural Ionodai High School"

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:17.250
The others seemed thrilled about getting fourth.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:21.950
But the captain and Kiriyama
looked so frustrated.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.700
From the day they placed fourth,
they got right back to training

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:29.200
determined to get first at nationals next time.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:34.830
I wanted to be a part of that.
I wanted to help them.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:42.250
But... I can't reach that level...
I'm not good enough...

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:45.250
Tomo, you wanted to confirm that...?

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:53.120
This is the last year for the captain
and Kiriyama. Get it?

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.080
So, you mean...

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.080
Ken.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.200
I'm counting on you.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:02.120
Isn't this a little cheap for a bribe?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.830
It's the best I can do right now.

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:08.330
Come on, you're ruining the moment.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.830
Thanks!

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:15.330
All right, I'm heading back first.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:26.540
I was rude earlier, Kiriyama, sir.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:28.580
I'm sorry.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.330
What's going on with Maeshima?

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.790
"Kensei Maeshima"     "Shotaro Terauchi"
"Akimitsu Mochizuki"
"Itsuki Kiriyama"     "Sota Jonouchi"

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.790
Ah, you mean his recent skating?

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:37.500
"Kensei Maeshima"     "Shotaro Terauchi"
"Akimitsu Mochizuki"
"Itsuki Kiriyama"     "Sota Jonouchi"

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:37.500
He's been using Tomo's skating as a reference.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:40.120
"Kensei Maeshima"     "Shotaro Terauchi"
"Akimitsu Mochizuki"

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:40.120
He says that for visualizing
the position of the wing and guards,

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.910
"Kensei Maeshima"     "Shotaro Terauchi"
"Akimitsu Mochizuki"
"Itsuki Kiriyama"     "Sota Jonouchi"

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.910
Tomo's skating is the best.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.080
"Kensei Maeshima"     "Shotaro Terauchi"
"Akimitsu Mochizuki"
"Itsuki Kiriyama"     "Sota Jonouchi"

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.080
Mine?

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:46.790
It's unusual for that idiot to use
someone else as a reference.

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:50.700
Isn't it that he finally gets
what skate-leading is all about?

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:54.410
If that's the case, he somehow made it
in time for the Grand Prix Series.

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:55.950
The outfits are ready, too.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:57.750
And we've improved the choreography.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:01.040
All right! First match of the Grand Prix Series!

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:04.250
We, Ionodai, will win and find our rhythm!

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:05.500
Yeah!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:40.080
"Next time" "Indecision"

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:43.330
"Next time" "Indecision"

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:43.330
Come on, you two. Why don't you talk aloud?

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:46.700
"Next time" "Indecision"

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:46.700
Didn't I just teach you about emotional
release and proper vocal use?

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.910
"Next time" "Indecision"

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.910
Right. Yes, sir!

00:23:47.910 --> 00:23:50.910
"Next time" "Indecision"

00:23:47.910 --> 00:23:50.910
Don't raise your voices all of a sudden.
